## Settled Direction

- Keep bare `ts: 100k` and generated `work/100k.md` read-only.
- Add `ts: 100k add <directive>` as the CEO command surface, with `ts: directive <directive>` as a concise alias.
- Persist a directive as an existing Idea Brief marked with role `project-executive-directive-v1`;
  do not add a directive table, backlog, queue, or lifecycle engine.
- Preserve the CEO's directive text and use the existing outcome, relationship, PRM, campaign, and
  evidence machinery as execution authority.
- Treat a directive as ready for Plan Cycle intake, not as a requirement that the CEO choose
  brainstorm, project-map, roadmap, or campaign mechanics.
- Continue automatically under the project-bound autonomy envelope. An explicit requested endpoint
  governs delivery; absent delivery language, source-changing directives stop at a verified Work1 candidate.
- Project directive state into 100k from canonical Idea/outcome/relationship state.
- Keep semantic truth visible: deterministic source freshness must not be described as proof that
  executive framing still matches released or runtime reality.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Directive authority | Portable directive template and managed Idea metadata using existing document primitives | document authority |
| Delegation route | Skill and operator contract hand the directive to PRM and preserve endpoint boundaries | directive authority |
| Executive visibility | 100k shows directive state and next subordinate handoff | shared project projection |
| Proof and current truth | Focused tests, docs, manifest integrity, and corrected current executive intent | prior workstreams |

## Program Shape

One bounded Work1 milestone implements the route, projection, tests, and documentation; corrects
the current executive intent after the v0.56.0 release; checkpoints the governed result; and stops
without deployment, push, release, or installed-client synchronization.

## Constraints And Non-Goals

- No second backlog, queue, database table, or lifecycle engine.
- No mutation from bare `ts: 100k` or from rendering the projection.
- No autonomous expansion or reinterpretation of the CEO's desired outcome.
- No production publication, remote deployment, or client synchronization in this milestone.
- No requirement that the CEO know artifact names or copy internal state tokens.

## Completion Boundary

The map is complete when the directive route, existing-substrate persistence, subordinate PRM
handoff, 100k visibility, current executive framing, portable tests, strict health, and checkpoint
rebuild parity pass in one locally committed Work1 candidate.
